52.16]] In propositione particulari affirmativa erunt tam <i>s</i> et <greek>p</greek> quam <greek>s</greek> et <i>p</i> primi inter se seu\n[[252.17]] nullum habentes divisorem communem. </p>\n<p> [[252.18]] Propositus sit syllogismus examinandus:\n [[252.19]] <i>Omnis sapiens est pius.</i> <tab/><i>sapiens</i> +70 ─33 <tab/><i>pius</i> +10 ─3\n [[252.20]] <i>Quidam sapiens est fortunatus.</i> <tab/><i>fortunatus</i> +8 ─11\n [[252.21]] <i>Ergo quidam <tab/>fortunatus est <tab/> pius.</i>\n [[252.22]] <tab/>+8 ─11 <tab/>+10 ─3\n [[252.23]] Quae conclusio procedit, quia neque 8 per 3 neque 11 per 10 dividi potest. </p>\n<p> [[253.1]] Aliter ista comminisci licet: considerandum nempe si animal est genus hominis,\n[[253.2]] contra: non-homo est genus non-animalis, itaque\n [[253.3]] <i>Nullus homo est</i> <i>lapis</i>\n [[253.4]] seu <i>Om<tab/>nis homo est n<tab/>on-lapis.</i>\n [[253.5]] Sit <tab/>+<i>h</i> ─<i>c</i> <tab/>1 ─<i>cd</i>\n [[253.6]] debet <i>h</i> dividi per 1, et <i>cd</i> dividi per <i>c</i>. </p>\n<p> [[253.7]] Hinc si dixas: <i>Omnis homo est corpus non lapis</i>, debet <i>hominis</i> numerus positivus\n[[253.8]] dividi posse per numerum <i>corporis</i>, at numerus <i>lapidis</i> debet dividi posse per numerum\n[[253.9]] <i>hominis</i> privativum.\n [[253.10]] <picture>157</picture> <tab/><picture>157</picture>\n [[253.11]] +<i>rs</i> ─<greek>rs</greek> aequ. +<i>xp</i> ─<greek>jp</greek>\n [[253.12]] Semper <Fn>Mutata aequatione in propositionem, nihil refert in subjecto qualisnam sit <greek>r</greek> neque in praedicato qualisnam sit <i>x</i>. Hinc si sit propositio: <i>Omnis homo est non lapis</i> inde fiet aequatio: ─<i>s</i> ─<greek>rs</greek> <i>aequ.</i> ─<greek>p</greek> +<i>xp</i> Ergo ─<i>s</i> +<greek>rs</greek> <i>aequ.</i> ─<i>xp</i> +<greek>p</greek></Fn> <i>rs</i> aequ. <i>xp</i> et <greek>rs</greek> aequ. <greek>jp</greek>, in propositione Universali erit <i>r</i> aequ. 1 et </p>\n<p> [[253.13]] <greek>j</greek> aequ. 1, in propositione Particulari erunt majora unitate. Hinc:\n [[253.14]] +<i>by aequ.</i> <tab/>─ <greek>by</greek> <tab/><i>da</i> ─<greek>da</greek>\n [[253.15]] +<i>ce</i> <tab/>─ <greek>ge</greek> [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[253.16]] In omni syllogismo est major minor medius.\n [[253.17]] In prima figura est\n [[253.18]] Medius Major <tab/>Minor Medius <tab/>Minor Major </p>\n<p> [[253.19]] seu Minor Medius <tab/>Medius Major <tab/>Minor Major\n [[253.20]] in secunda:\n [[253.21]] Medius Major <tab/>Medius Minor <tab/>Minor Major\n [[253.22]] in tertia:\n [[253.23]] Major Medius <tab/>Minor Medius <tab/>Minor Major </p>\n<p> [[254.1]] Sit minor <i>y</i>, Medius <i>e</i>, Major <i>a</i>,\n [[254.2]] fiat\n [[254.3]] 1) <i>by</i> <i>aequ. ce</i> <tab/> 2) <greek>by</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <greek>ge</greek>\n [[254.4]] 3) <i>fe</i> <i>aequ. da</i> <tab/> 4) <greek>fe</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <greek>da</greek>\n [[254.5]] 5) <i>ly aequ. ma</i> <tab/> 6) <greek>ly</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <greek>ma</greek>\n [[254.6]] Ergo\n [[254.7]] 7) <zl><i>y</i> <ne><i>e</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>c</i> <ne><i>b</i> <be> <tab/> 8) <zl><greek>y</greek> <ne><greek>e</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>g</greek> <ne><greek>b</greek> <be>\n [[254.8]] 9) <zl><i>e</i> <ne><i>a</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>d</i> <ne><i>f</i> <be> <tab/>10) <zl><greek>e</greek> <ne><greek>a</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>d</greek> <ne><greek>f</greek> <be>\n [[254.9]] 11) <zl><i>y</i> <ne><i>a</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>m</i> <ne> <i>l</i> <be> <tab/>12) <zl><greek>y</greek> <ne><greek>a</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>m</greek> <ne><greek>l</greek> <be>\n [[254.10]] Ergo per 7 et 9 fit\n [[254.11]] 13) <zl><i>y</i> <ne><i>a</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>cd</i> <ne><i>bf</i> <be>\n [[254.12]] adeoque per 11\n [[254.13]] 14) <zl><i>cd</i> <ne><i>bf</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>m</i> <ne> <i>l</i> <be> .\n [[254.14]] Eodemque modo per 8 et 10\n [[254.15]] <tab/>15) <zl><greek>y</greek> <ne><greek>a</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>gd</greek> <ne><greek>bf</greek> <be>\n [[254.16]] seu per 12\n [[254.17]] <tab/>16) <zl><greek>gd</greek> <ne><greek>bf</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>m</greek> <ne><greek>l</greek> <be>\n [[254.18]] Rursus jungendo 7 et 11 fiet:\n [[254.19]] 17) <zl><i>a</i> <ne><i>e</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl> <i>cl</i> <ne><i>bm</i> <be>\n [[254.20]] seu per 9 fiet\n [[254.21]] 18) <zl><i>f</i> <ne><i>d</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl> <i>cl</i> <ne><i>bm</i> <be> ,\n [[254.22]] sed haec aequatio 18 non differt ab aequatione 14.\n [[255.1]] 19) <i>y aequ.</i> <zl><i>c</i> <ne><i>b</i> <be> <i>e</i>\n [[255.2]] et\n [[255.3]] 20) <i>y aequ.</i> <zl><i>m</i> <ne><i> l</i> <be> <i>a</i>.\n [[255.4]] Ergo\n [[255.5]] 21) <zl><i>c</i> <ne><i>b</i> <be> <i>e aequ.</i> <zl><i>m</i> <ne> <i>l</i> <be> <i>a</i>\n [[255.6]] seu\n [[255.7]] 22) <i>a aequ.</i> <zl> <i>cl</i> <ne><i>mb</i> <be> <i>e</i>.\n [[255.8]] Hinc unus Terminus semper sumi poterit pro arbitrio.\n [[255.9]] Sumatur medius <i>e</i>, pro arbitrio,\n [[255.10]] <zl><i>bf</i> <ne><i>cd</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl> <i>l</i> <ne><i>m</i> <be>\n[[255.11]] <zl><i>minor b medius f</i> <ne><i>medius c major d</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl> <i>minor l</i> <ne><i>major m</i> <be> <zl><greek>bf</greek> <ne><greek>gd</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>l</greek> <ne><greek>m</greek> <be>\n [[255.12]] <i>y aequ.</i> <zl><i>c</i> <ne><i>b</i> <be> <i>e</i> <tab/> <greek>y</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>g</greek> <ne><greek>b</greek> <be> <greek>e</greek>\n [[255.13]] <i>a aequ.</i> <zl><i>f</i> <ne><i>d</i> <be> <i>e</i> <tab/> <greek>a</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><greek>f</greek> <ne><greek>d</greek> <be> <greek>e</greek>\n [[255.14]] Itaque ex datis sex aequationibus habemus sex alias.\n [[255.15]] <tab/>Minor <tab/>Medius <tab/>Major\n [[255.16]] <tab/><picture>8012</picture> <tab/><picture>8012</picture> <tab/><picture>8012</picture>\n [[255.17]] <tab/>+<i>y</i> ─<greek>y</greek> <tab/>+<i>e</i> ─<greek>e</greek> <tab/>+<i>a</i> ─<greek>a</greek>\n [[255.18]] <tab/><picture>166</picture><tab/><picture>167</picture> <tab/><picture>167</picture>\n [[256.1]] U. A. +<i>rs aequ. xp</i> <tab/>+<greek>rs</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <greek>jp</greek> <tab/>erit <i>r aequ.</i> 1 et <greek>r</greek> <i>aequ.</i> 1\n [[256.2]] P. N. <tab/>erit <i>r</i> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> 1 vel <greek>r</greek> ^&.zc <Leibniz special character> 1\n [[256.3]] P. A. <tab/>erunt <zl><i>r</i> <ne><greek>j</greek> <be> et <zl><greek>r</greek> <ne><i>x</i> <be> primi inter se, item\n [[256.4]] U. N. <tab/>erunt alterutri non primi inter se\n [[256.5]] vel sic:\n [[256.6]] <i>Rrs aequ. Xxp</i> <tab/>et <tab/><greek>Rrs</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <greek>Jjp</greek>\n [[256.7]] in U. A. <tab/>erit <i>Rr aequ.</i> <greek>Rr</greek> <i>aequ.</i> 1\n [[256.8]] in P. N. <tab/>contra alterutrum\n [[256.9]] in U. N. <tab/>erit <i>r aequ.</i> <greek>j</greek> vel <i>x aequ.</i> <greek>r</greek> </p>\n<p> [[256.10]] Itaque in superioribus scribemus:\n [[256.11]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character>Quart. fig. <tab/><i>e</i> <tab/><i>a</i> <tab/>Major <tab/> <i>D</i> <tab/>Quart. fig. <tab/><i>y</i> <tab/><i>e</i> <tab/> <i>Bby aequ. Cce</i> <tab/>Minor^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/> <tab/> <tab/> <tab/>\n [[256.12]] Prim. fig. <tab/><i>e a</i> <tab/>Prim. fig. <tab/><i>y e</i> <tab/> <i>Bby aequ. Cce</i> <tab/>Minor\n [[256.13]] Sec. fig. <tab/><i>e a</i> <tab/>Major <tab/> <i>Dda aequ. Ffe</i> <tab/>Sec. fig. <tab/><i>e y</i> <tab/><hebrew>b</i><greek>by</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <hebrew>g</i><greek>ge</greek>\n [[256.14]] Tert. fig. <tab/><i>a e</i> <tab/><hebrew>d</i><greek>da</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <hebrew>p</i><greek>fe</greek> <tab/>Tert. fig. <tab/><i>y e</i>\n [[256.15]] Quart. fig. <tab/><i>a e</i> <tab/>Quart. fig. <tab/><i>e y</i>\n [[256.16]] <tab/>Conclusio <tab/> <i>Lly aequ. Mma</i>\n [[256.17]] <tab/><hebrew>l</i><greek>ly</greek> <i>aequ.</i> <hebrew>m</i><greek>ma</greek>\n [[256.18]] <zl><i>CcDd</i> <ne><i>BbFf</i> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><i>Mm</i> <ne> <i>Ll</i> <be> <zl><hebrew>g</i><greek>g</greek><hebrew>d</i><greek>d</greek> <ne><hebrew>b</i><greek>b</greek><hebrew>p</i><greek>f</greek> <be> <i>aequ.</i> <zl><hebrew>m</i><greek>m</greek> <ne><hebrew>l</i><greek>l</greek> <be>\n [[256.19]] Prima figura: Medius major <tab/>Secunda figura: <tab/>Medius major\n [[256.20]] <tab/>minor medius <tab/>Medius minor\n [[256.21]] <tab/>Minor major <tab/>Minor Major\n [[256.22]] Tertia figura: <tab/>Major Medius <tab/>Quarta figura: <tab/>Major medius\n [[256.23]] <tab/>minor medius <tab/>medius minor\n [[256.24]] <tab/>Minor Major <tab/>minor major </p>\n<p> [[256.25]] Ex hoc calculo omnes modi et figurae derivari possunt per solas regulas Numerorum.\n[[256.26]] Si nosse volumus an aliqua figura procedat vi formae, videmus an contradictorium\n[[256.27]] conclusionis sit compatibile cum praemissis, id est an numeri reperiri possint satisfacientes\n[[256.28]] simul praemissis et contradictoriae conclusionis; quodsi nulli reperiri possunt concludet\n[[256.29]] argumentum vi formae. </p>\n",
